  "idea": "CapCut vs Premiere Pro: is professional editing software still necessary",
  "text": "Professional video editors are quietly ditching Adobe Premiere to build short-form client reels inside CapCut. High-paying clients demand rapid turnarounds, but Premiere's sluggish UI and crashed caption engines kill your margins. Building dynamic subtitles requires heavy MOGRT templates that bloat project files and stall timeline scrub speeds. CapCut delivers native word-by-word caption animations, instant vocal isolation, and cloud asset syncing without plugins. You scale monthly client capacity effortlessly.",
